# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Range-distribution reshard (tablet split / merge).
#
# These exist because a forced split finishes in well under a second, so no external fault
# (an FE restart takes ~17s) can land inside RUNNING. Arm one WITH PAUSE to freeze the job at
# that phase, act externally, then ADMIN DISABLE FAILPOINT to release.
#
# Where a pause parks -- read this before arming one:
#   * All six rules below park the SINGLE TabletReshardJobMgr daemon thread, which runs
#     ColocateChecker.runOneCycle(), drainReshardCandidates() and runTabletReshardJobs() in
#     sequence. So any one of them freezes every reshard job AND colocate convergence on that
#     frontend, and only one can be in effect at a time. The daemon loop has no watchdog, so a
#     park just means missed ticks.
#   * NEVER write a rule inside SplitTabletJob/MergeTabletJob.addNewMaterializedIndexes: it holds
#     the table WRITE lock, so parking there makes the table unavailable to queries and DDL for
#     the whole pause. The two *_before_metadata_switch rules below deliberately sit at the CALL
#     to it, which is outside every lock.
#
# Every DO is a safe no-op, so arming one of these with ENABLE instead of PAUSE skips one daemon
# tick rather than corrupting a job.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Generic amplifier: hold any reshard job at its current state so an external fault (kill a CN,
# switch the leader, partition the network) lands while the job is still in flight. Note run()
# catches Exception and aborts the job, so DO throw here would inject a job FAILURE, not a pause.
RULE tablet_reshard_job_run
CLASS com.starrocks.alter.reshard.TabletReshardJob
METHOD run()
HELPER com.starrocks.failpoint.FailPointHelper
IF shouldTrigger("tablet_reshard_job_run")
DO return;
ENDRULE

# Split points computed and the split transaction published, catalog NOT yet switched. Kill the
# leader here and the follower must take over with the tablet set and ranges exactly as before.
RULE split_before_metadata_switch
CLASS com.starrocks.alter.reshard.SplitTabletJob
METHOD runRunningJob
AT INVOKE addNewMaterializedIndexes
HELPER com.starrocks.failpoint.FailPointHelper
IF shouldTrigger("split_before_metadata_switch")
DO return;
ENDRULE

# Merge peer of split_before_metadata_switch.
RULE merge_before_metadata_switch
CLASS com.starrocks.alter.reshard.MergeTabletJob
METHOD runRunningJob
AT INVOKE addNewMaterializedIndexes
HELPER com.starrocks.failpoint.FailPointHelper
IF shouldTrigger("merge_before_metadata_switch")
DO return;
ENDRULE

# Catalog switched and the CLEANING transition already journalled (setJobState writes
# logUpdateTabletReshardJob), job not yet FINISHED. Restart here and replay must be idempotent:
# ranges contiguous, no overlap, no duplicate tablet id.
RULE split_after_metadata_switch
CLASS com.starrocks.alter.reshard.SplitTabletJob
METHOD runCleaningJob
AT ENTRY
HELPER com.starrocks.failpoint.FailPointHelper
IF shouldTrigger("split_after_metadata_switch")
DO return;
ENDRULE

# Merge peer of split_after_metadata_switch.
RULE merge_after_metadata_switch
CLASS com.starrocks.alter.reshard.MergeTabletJob
METHOD runCleaningJob
AT ENTRY
HELPER com.starrocks.failpoint.FailPointHelper
IF shouldTrigger("merge_after_metadata_switch")
DO return;
ENDRULE

# Colocate cross-table alignment, per table. AT EXIT, not AT ENTRY: the trigger has no table
# predicate or call counter, so an armed PAUSE stops the FIRST invocation of the cycle. At ENTRY that
# would mean no table was processed at all -- a not-started group, not a mid-alignment one. At EXIT the
# first table of the group has been processed (its alignment job fired, if it needed one) and the next
# has not, which is the partially-processed state "fail-close or full rollback" must be asserted
# against. Note the fired job cannot run while this rule is parked: it would run on this same daemon
# thread. false is what the method already returns for "work still needed, retry next cycle".
RULE colocate_mid_align_table
CLASS com.starrocks.alter.reshard.ColocateChecker
METHOD alignTableIfApplicable
AT EXIT
HELPER com.starrocks.failpoint.FailPointHelper
IF shouldTrigger("colocate_mid_align_table")
DO return false;
ENDRULE


# ============================== Iceberg ==============================
# Nothing in this file touched the Iceberg connector before. The concurrency bugs that keep
# showing up there -- commit conflicts, caches handing out paths an external engine already
# expired, partition-spec evolution racing with DML -- all live in windows a few milliseconds
# wide, so a random concurrent workload only hits them by luck. These four turn those windows
# into something a test can stop inside.

# The transaction carries the new snapshot and nothing is published yet: the window a competing
# commit has to land in to produce "Base metadata location is not same".
#
# The site has to be read together with what the callers do. All three of them pass
# commitWithCleanup a lambda shaped like
#
#     rowDelta.commit();              // stages the snapshot into the transaction
#     publishStagedTransaction(tx);   // publishes it
#
# so the entry of commitWithCleanup -- where this rule used to sit -- is *before* the staging,
# and stopping there exercises a different race than the one described above. The window we want
# is between those two statements, and publishStagedTransaction exists to give it a name.
#
# Deliberately on StarRocks' own method rather than on iceberg's Transaction.commitTransaction,
# which would be one frame tighter: a rule naming a class that does not resolve, or a signature
# that drifted with the library version, is silently dead -- ADMIN ENABLE FAILPOINT reports
# success for a rule that will never fire. Naming the synthetic lambda$...$N that holds the two
# statements fails the same way on any edit to IcebergMetadata. Only rules over named code in
# this repo can be kept honest by a compile, and FailPointBtmRuleTest checks this signature.
RULE iceberg_commit_before_metadata_swap
CLASS com.starrocks.connector.iceberg.IcebergMetadata
METHOD publishStagedTransaction(Transaction)
AT ENTRY
HELPER com.starrocks.failpoint.FailPointHelper
IF shouldTrigger("iceberg_commit_before_metadata_swap")
DO sleep(5000);
ENDRULE

# The file list is resolved and about to be handed to the backends, but no backend has opened
# anything yet. Arm this, run an expire/rewrite from another engine inside the pause, and the
# scan is forced to read a list that no longer matches storage.
#
# ONLY FIRES UNDER `set enable_connector_incremental_scan_ranges = false`. That session variable
# defaults to **true**, and IcebergScanNode.setupScanRangeLocations then calls
# getRemoteFilesAsync, a separate implementation that does not delegate to this method. Byteman
# installs this rule either way and ADMIN ENABLE FAILPOINT reports success, so an armed pause
# that never happens is this variable, not a broken rule. For the default path use
# iceberg_scan_source_built below -- it is a different window, not this one reached another way.
RULE iceberg_scan_files_planned
CLASS com.starrocks.connector.iceberg.IcebergMetadata
METHOD getRemoteFiles(Table, GetRemoteFilesParams)
AT EXIT
HELPER com.starrocks.failpoint.FailPointHelper
IF shouldTrigger("iceberg_scan_files_planned")
DO sleep(5000);
ENDRULE

# The default scan path, because enable_connector_incremental_scan_ranges defaults to true.
#
# This is a **different** window from iceberg_scan_files_planned, not the same one reached by
# another route. The async source is lazy: buildRemoteInfoSource wraps a
# CloseableIterator<FileScanTask> and produces files one at a time as the backends consume them,
# so "the whole list is resolved" is a state that never exists here. AT EXIT means: the source is
# built and not one FileScanTask has been produced. That is enough to race an expire/rewrite
# against planning, which is the family this exists for -- it is not the stronger guarantee that
# a complete, already-resolved list is in hand.
RULE iceberg_scan_source_built
CLASS com.starrocks.connector.iceberg.IcebergMetadata
METHOD getRemoteFilesAsync(Table, GetRemoteFilesParams)
AT EXIT
HELPER com.starrocks.failpoint.FailPointHelper
IF shouldTrigger("iceberg_scan_source_built")
DO sleep(5000);
ENDRULE

# The cached table is known to be stale (metadata file location differs) and the swap to the
# new one has not happened yet. Holds the per-table refresh monitor, which is the point: it is
# what a second refresh of the same table has to contend with.
RULE iceberg_cache_refresh_before_swap
CLASS com.starrocks.connector.iceberg.CachingIcebergCatalog
METHOD refreshTable(BaseTable, BaseTable, String, String, ConnectContext, ExecutorService)
AT ENTRY
HELPER com.starrocks.failpoint.FailPointHelper
IF shouldTrigger("iceberg_cache_refresh_before_swap")
DO sleep(5000);
ENDRULE

# Every ALTER clause has been applied to the transaction and the transaction is not committed
# yet. For Iceberg that means a new PartitionSpec is staged but not published -- the window
# concurrent DML has to be in to observe a spec that is about to change underneath it.
# Defined on the shared connector executor, so it fires for any connector ALTER, not only
# Iceberg; there is no Iceberg-only method at this phase.
RULE connector_alter_clauses_applied
CLASS com.starrocks.connector.ConnectorAlterTableExecutor
METHOD applyClauses()
AT EXIT
HELPER com.starrocks.failpoint.FailPointHelper
IF shouldTrigger("connector_alter_clauses_applied")
DO sleep(5000);
ENDRULE

# The other side of the same ALTER: transaction.commitTransaction() has returned, so the new
# metadata -- a new PartitionSpec, for the evolution case -- is published, and the frontend
# cache still holds the old table. IcebergMetadata.alterTable does not refresh it until this
# method returns, so a query planned inside the pause plans against a spec that storage has
# already moved past. connector_alter_clauses_applied stops before the commit; this one stops
# after. Between them the spec switch is deterministic instead of a millisecond race.
#
# No catalog lock is held: alterTable's synchronized(this) block starts after the executor
# returns, which is after this rule has already fired.
#
# AT EXIT does not fire on the throw path (Byteman triggers on return, not athrow), so an
# ALTER that failed to commit does not pause -- which is what we want, there is nothing
# published to be stale against.
RULE iceberg_alter_published_before_refresh
CLASS com.starrocks.connector.iceberg.IcebergAlterTableExecutor
METHOD applyClauses()
AT EXIT
HELPER com.starrocks.failpoint.FailPointHelper
IF shouldTrigger("iceberg_alter_published_before_refresh")
DO sleep(5000);
ENDRULE

# HMS 连接池 —— 元数据服务是数据湖的单点依赖,而它"拿不到连接"和"连不上"是两回事:
# 后者网络层能造,前者只在 FE 进程内部(池满 / 建连被 HMS 拒),外面看不见。
#
# 作用域: **只覆盖 Hive connector, 不覆盖 Iceberg**。getClient() 是 HiveMetaClient 内部
# 所有到 metastore 路径的必经之处(callRPC 和 getPartitionsByNames 两类调用都走它),
# 但它是 HiveMetaClient 的 private 方法, 调用方全在该类内部。Iceberg Hive catalog
# 不经过这里: IcebergHiveCatalog 持有 org.apache.iceberg.hive.HiveCatalog 作为 delegate,
# 元数据操作走 iceberg 自己的 client pool。所以这两条 armed 之后, Iceberg 的表加载与
# 提交不会被注入 —— 原因见 README 的 "Known gap: Iceberg's own HMS connection acquisition" 一节。
# ⚠ 危险度最高的两条: 可能持锁 5s, 后果是**导入失败**而不是查询变慢。
# getClient() 第一句是 BlockingCallValidator.validateNotUnderLock(...), 它是**探测器而非保证**:
# 只在持锁时上报, 从不阻止调用, Mode.OFF 下连报都不报。它装在这里恰恰说明
# 这条路径可能在锁下被走—— LockInvariantViolations 写明 blocking-call 规则的违规集
# "还在收集中"(still collecting), 即已知存在持锁调 HMS 的站点且未全部修复。
# transaction publish 取表锁用的是 1000ms tryLock, 所以这里 sleep 5s 一旦落在持锁路径上,
# 等在那把锁上的导入会成批失败(5 倍于 tryLock 预算)。
#
# 开之前先查: FE 日志 grep blocking_call_under_lock 且 transport=hive-metastore,
# 你的负载下为空才说明这条路径当前没在锁下。详见 README 同名小节。
#
# 另: 两条都是 AT ENTRY, sleep 在 validator 之前, 所以解释卡顿的
# LOCK_INVARIANT_VIOLATION 日志会晚 5s 才出现 —— 它是 5 秒前那次卡顿的因, 不是果。
RULE hms_client_pool_exhausted
CLASS com.starrocks.connector.hive.HiveMetaClient
METHOD getClient
AT ENTRY
HELPER com.starrocks.failpoint.FailPointHelper
IF shouldTrigger("hms_client_pool_exhausted")
DO throw new org.apache.hadoop.hive.metastore.api.MetaException("failpoint: could not connect to meta store, connection pool exhausted");
ENDRULE

# 建连很慢(HMS 在 GC 停顿 / 排队)。和网络层的延迟注入不同:这条不需要 root,
# 也只影响 SR 到 HMS 这一段,不碰 BE 之间的 RPC。
RULE hms_client_acquire_slow
CLASS com.starrocks.connector.hive.HiveMetaClient
METHOD getClient
AT ENTRY
HELPER com.starrocks.failpoint.FailPointHelper
IF shouldTrigger("hms_client_acquire_slow")
DO sleep(5000);
ENDRULE
